From 6b36139e5804052213c04aa386a8895c34763c18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:47:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] arm64: dts: apple: pass the country to the Wi-Fi firmware

The Broadcom firmware on Apple boards takes ISO 3166 country codes with
revision 0: its CLM blob has an entry for each country, and setting
ccode=PL (no regrev) in the NVRAM is accepted. Mark every Apple
Broadcom Wi-Fi node with brcm,ccode-map-trivial so brcmfmac passes the
regulatory domain to the firmware instead of leaving it on the NVRAM's
worldwide ccode=XZ.

The t602x boards inherit the property from the t600x nodes they
override. The t8140 Wi-Fi is not Broadcom and is left alone.

Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
